# Doom Foretold on turn 3, when Bot2 controls a land (Plains), a Servo token and three nonland, nontoken permanents (Retrofitter
# Foundry, Mox Pearl, Mox Jet). At Bot2's upkeep Bot2 must sacrifice one of the three (the land and the token are not offered),
# so none of the "if that player can't" effects happen: no life lost or gained, no Knight, the enchantment stays. At Bot1's own
# upkeep Bot1 (the controller) must sacrifice too, among four Moxen and the enchantment itself, never its Plains: it sacrifices
# Doom Foretold for its own ability (the ruling), and having sacrificed, it draws nothing and makes no Knight. CR 701.21a,
# 111.1, 608.2c.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Doom Foretold
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Retrofitter Foundry
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

